# Everything here is excluded from the build context sent to the daemon.
# Two reasons, both load-bearing:
#   1. Secrets (.env) must never enter an image layer -- layers are extractable.
#   2. A smaller context means faster builds and fewer spurious cache busts.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules

# build output -- the image builds its own, never copies a host build
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Prisma's generated client. MUST be excluded: it contains a platform-specific
# query engine binary. A developer on Debian generates a ~17MB
# debian-openssl-3.0.x engine; copying that into an Alpine image ships a
# binary that can never load, next to the musl one the build generates. Worse,
# it makes the image contents depend on the host that built it.
**/generated

# caches
.turbo
**/.turbo
.pnpm-store
**/.vite

# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# tests / e2e artifacts
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
blob-report
**/blob-report

# docs and scratch -- not needed to build a binary
docs
temp
*.md
!README.md

# editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
